### Test DynamoDB API Endpoints

### 1. Check database status
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/test/database-status

### 2. Test DynamoDB user creation (via test endpoint)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/test/dynamo/test-user
Content-Type: application/json

### 3. Test DynamoDB signup
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/test/dynamo/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "testpassword123",
  "passwordConfirm": "testpassword123"
}

### 4. Test DynamoDB login
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/test/dynamo/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "testpassword123"
}

### 5. Test protected route (use token from login response)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/test/protected
Cookie: jwt=your-jwt-token-here

### 6. Compare with MongoDB signup (if MongoDB is running)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/test/mongo/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Doe",
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
  "password": "testpassword123",
  "passwordConfirm": "testpassword123"
}